{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfrz7egWWZEXbVRmgvpeR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`jsonpatch/core.py` is implemented per the spec, and all 42 tests in `tests/test_core.py` pass with `python3 -m unittest tests.test_core`.\n\n**Implementation**\n- `resolve_pointer` handles `\"\"` as the whole document, unescapes `~1` before `~0`, and enforces the array index rules (no leading zeros, `-` rejected). Anything invalid raises `PointerError`.\n- `apply_patch` runs every operation on a deep copy, so a failure anywhere leaves the input untouched. Copied and inserted values are deep-copied too, so the output never aliases the patch.\n- `test` uses type-aware equality: numbers compare by value and `True != 1`.\n\n**Choices where the spec was silent**\n- `remove` on the root raises `PatchError`, since there is no document left afterwards.\n- `replace` on the root is allowed.\n- `move` with `from` as the root (`\"\"`) is rejected. The \"proper prefix\" rule catches it, and the root can't be removed anyway.\n- `in_place=True` mutates the original dict or list when the result is the same container type. If the root is replaced with a different type, it can't be mutated in place, so the new value is returned and the original is left alone.\n\n**Tests**\n- Written with `unittest` so they need no new dependency. The run command is `python3 -m unittest tests.test_core`. Plain `unittest discover` fails here because `tests/` has no `__init__.py`.\n- One test failed on the first run because the fixture was wrong: I had keyed the test document with `~0` where RFC 6901 requires `~`. I fixed the fixture, not the code.\n\nI did not commit anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4688,"cache_read_input_tokens":60243,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4688},"output_token